+
+## Passkeys
+
+Readers can sign up, sign in, and reauthenticate with passkeys (WebAuthn), and manage them from `/account`.
+
+- Password sign-in/sign-up are proxied through `/api/auth/*`, so the server can keep a signed-in session.
+- Passkey public keys are stored in `.data/passkeys.json` (override with `PASSKEY_DB_PATH`).
+- The relying party ID and allowed origins come from the request URL. Pin them with `WEBAUTHN_RP_ID` and `WEBAUTHN_ORIGINS` (comma-separated) if needed.
+- Adding or removing a passkey requires the user to have signed in or reauthenticated within the last 5 minutes.
